---
// The Pangea board on /projects: four random-move bots partway through a game
// on the Earth map, drawn by the game's own renderer at
// pangea.akan72.workers.dev/embed. That page takes no input, opens no saves
// and calls no API, and it's outside the game's Cloudflare Access login. The
// frame ignores the pointer, so the whole board is one link to the game, the
// page scrolls over it, and site/scripts/screensaver.js still sees the mouse.
// The project's name already links there, so this link is decorative: out of
// the tab order and hidden from screen readers and the page's Markdown copy.
---
<a class="pangea-embed" href="https://pangea.akan72.workers.dev/" target="_blank" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <iframe
        src="https://pangea.akan72.workers.dev/embed"
        title="Pangea: four random-move bots partway through a game on the Earth map"
        loading="lazy"
        referrerpolicy="no-referrer"
        tabindex="-1"
    ></iframe>
</a>

<style>
    /* Same 536px width as the Vesta board and the mingus map. The Earth map is
       2.3 times as wide as it is tall, so this frame leaves no margins. */
    .pangea-embed { display: block; width: 536px; max-width: 100%; margin: 1em 0; }
    iframe {
        display: block; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 2.3 / 1; border: 0;
        pointer-events: none;
        /* The map's deep-sea color, so the frame doesn't flash while it loads */
        background: #1d3a52;
    }
</style>
